{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The baseline no-show fee is chargeable only if all four POL-NS-01 conditions hold, and limb (c) fails on the driver's own telemetry. The pickup zone class is STANDARD (trip_record.pickup_zone_class), so the required continuous in-geofence dwell is 300 seconds, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix rather than from the 'arrived' tap. The trace's longest qualifying in-geofence run is 240 seconds, from 2026-09-23T15:12:50 to 15:16:50, and its accumulated in-geofence dwell is 230 seconds - a shortfall of 70 seconds. Because the driver did not hold position for the required minimum, limb (c) is broken and the fee is not chargeable under this clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00708", "EV-TRIP-00708"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06 then directs the remedy: where the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the POL-NS-01 minimum for the zone class, the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider answered messages. Required 300 seconds for STANDARD, measured 240 seconds (accumulated 230), shortfall 70 seconds as computed on the trace. The only qualification, limb (i) accumulation, is unavailable here: EV-ADVIS-00708-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, and POL-NS-06(i) requires a present and populated advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT before separate in-geofence intervals may be summed. No advisory exists, so nothing bridges the shortfall and nothing excuses it. The charge is refunded in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00708", "EV-TRIP-00708", "EV-ADVIS-00708-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) of POL-NS-01 fails as well. The trip record shows cancellation_reason_code null, cancelled_by null, cancelled_at null and status COMPLETED. There is no termination by the driver on RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and no boarding event is recorded anywhere on the trip. The driver's own counterparty statement does not assert that anyone boarded - it says the passengers 'were confused and walked away'. With limb (d) unsatisfied, no no-show fee is chargeable under POL-NS-01 at all, and the charge taken from the rider cannot stand as an itemised cancellation fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00708"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.counterparty_statement",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 independently exonerates the rider and refunds the fee in full with no driver compensation payable. Limb (a): the chat log holds the rider's message sent at 2026-09-23T15:16:50 - 'My parents are still at the pickup. Did anyone board?' - which is both a statement of the riders' position and a request for the driver's position, and it was sent while the driver was still inside the geofence, his qualifying run ending at the same moment. Limb (b): the driver neither replied in the chat within 120 seconds of that message nor placed any in-app voice call - trip_record.in_app_calls is empty - before the trip ended at 15:20:40. Limb (c) cannot be run at all because the trace carries no rider track (rider_fix_count 0), and POL-NS-04 makes an absent rider track UNDECIDABLE and neutral: it is expressly neither satisfied nor failed, and the Judge must not infer from it that the rider was elsewhere. On limbs (a) and (b), with (c) neutral, the fee is refunded in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00708", "EV-TRIP-00708", "EV-GPS-00708"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.last_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The sum actually taken is not a no-show fee, and I disclose the impairment rather than present it clean: EV-FARE-00708 carries weight_multiplier 0.6 and issue code UNVERIFIED_SOURCE (MAJOR) - a manually transcribed rider payment screen with no independent ledger corroboration, which the driver also disputes. On its face it shows cancellation_fee 0.00 alongside total_charged 26.00, composed of base_fare 3.80, distance_fare 14.90, time_fare 6.50 and platform_fee 0.80: a completed-trip fare, not a cancellation fee, and its own money derivation reports a schedule fee of 4.00 against a fee charged of 0.00. Even on the driver's best case, the chargeable no-show fee for a STANDARD RYDE_X trip under POL-NS-01 and fee_schedule.resolution_rule is the greater of the zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) - SGD 4.00. The rider should not be left carrying a completed-trip fare for a trip on which no passenger boarded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00708", "EV-TRIP-00708"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, if the amount cannot be fixed because the only ledger for it is the impaired, unverified fare screen that both parties dispute, the case cannot be decided on the money and must escalate under POL-NS-09: the sole evidence for the deciding amount is impaired and the conflict is unresolved by any clause. POL-GEN-02 permits ESCALATE where a deciding fact rests solely on an artifact at or below weight 0.65, as here. Escalation holds the disputed SGD 26 rather than collecting or refunding it, so the rider is not left carrying a charge the platform cannot substantiate. Either way the rider should not bear this charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00708"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}

