  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver, here is the decision.\n\nWHAT WE ACCEPT. The driver did reach the pickup and wait there — EV-GPS-00708 shows 25 qualifying in-geofence fixes with a closest approach of 1.24 m to the pin — but he did not wait long enough. His longest continuous stay inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius was 240 seconds (accumulated in-geofence dwell 230 s) against the 300-second minimum the no-show rules require, a shortfall of 70 seconds as the trace's own derivation computes it. His arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: nothing in the trace places him more than 300 m from the pin, or moving at 15 km/h or above, at the moment he tapped 'arrived'. And EV-TRIP-00708 shows the trip was never closed out as a no-show at all — status COMPLETED, cancellation_reason_code null, cancelled_by null, cancelled_at null. So no no-show fee was chargeable: POL-NS-01 limbs (c) and (d) both fail.\n\nWHY THAT DOES NOT PRODUCE A REFUND. The amount charged, SGD 26.00, is not a no-show fee. EV-FARE-00708 records a cancellation-fee line of 0.00, and the platform's own money derivation records a fee charged of 0.00; the 26.00 is itemised as base fare 3.80 + distance fare 14.90 + time fare 6.50 + platform fee 0.80 — an ordinary completed-trip fare. POL-NS-06 refunds the cancellation-fee line and nothing else, and expressly not the booking or platform items that belong to a completed trip. There is no cancellation fee here to refund, and the most a no-show fee could ever have been on this trip — the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee of 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of 4.00, i.e. 4.00 — was never levied. The rider's claim for the return of the SGD 26.00 therefore cannot be supported under this category, and the charge stands as it presently is (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The outcome is NO_ACTION.\n\nON THE ARGUMENTS. The rider's points that POL-NS-01 limb (c) fails (240 s against 300 s, a 70 s shortfall) and limb (d) fails (no termination on RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT) are accepted, and so is the rider's observation that the 26.00 is a completed-trip fare rather than a no-show fee. Those findings are what deny the driver any compensation, but they return no money, because POL-NS-06 refunds only the cancellation-fee line and that line is 0.00. The rider's POL-NS-04 argument is rejected: the single chat message was sent at 15:16:50, ten seconds after the trip started at 15:16:40, so it was not sent 'during the waiting window' as limb (a) requires, and limb (c) cannot be run at all because the trace carries no rider track (rider_fix_count 0) — and in any event POL-NS-04 would also refund only the cancellation-fee line. The driver's points that the driver arrived and held, that the arrival marker is not a false arrival, that POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider, and that no cancellation fee was ever charged are accepted. The driver's conditional request to escalate if the amount cannot be fixed is rejected: NO_ACTION does not require the disputed amount to be fixed, and the deciding fact — that this was a completed trip, not a no-show — is carried independently and at full weight by EV-TRIP-00708, not solely by the fare screen.\n\nEVIDENCE WEIGHTING. EV-FARE-00708 is impaired — weight 0.6, issue code UNVERIFIED_SOURCE (MAJOR), a manually transcribed rider payment screen with no independent ledger corroboration, which the driver expressly disputes — and it is named here for that reason. The ruling does not rest on it: EV-TRIP-00708, at full weight 1.0, independently shows the trip was completed and never cancelled, so confidence is not capped at 0.6 and the impairment does not force escalation under POL-NS-09(a) or (e). Confidence 0.85.\n\nNO REFERRAL is entered: no clause produces one on these facts. The POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival referral does not fire because qualifying in-geofence fixes do exist, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination in 30 days against 110 completed trips).\n\nONE OPEN POINT FOR THE RIDER, not a referral: if the completed-trip fare of 26.00 was taken although no passenger ever boarded, that is a completed-trip fare dispute, which is a different category from this no-show dispute. Nothing in the no-show policy decides it, and this ruling does not decide it."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "In the alternative, if the amount cannot be fixed because the only ledger for it is the impaired, unverified fare screen that both parties dispute, the case cannot be decided on the money and must escalate under POL-NS-09: the sole evidence for the deciding amount is impaired and the conflict is unresolved by any clause. POL-GEN-02 permits ESCALATE where a deciding fact rests solely on an artifact at or below weight 0.65, as here. Escalation holds the disputed SGD 26 rather than collecting or refunding it, so the rider is not left carrying a charge the platform cannot substantiate. Either way the rider should not bear this charge.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-FARE-00708 at weight_multiplier 0.6 but does not name its issue code(s): UNVERIFIED_SOURCE"
    }
  ]
}

